  "summary": "'ve spent 20 years building enterprise fabrication-management software, most recently leading development on Tekla PowerFab at Trimble.\n\nMy focus over the years has shifted from hands-on integration work to developing the people who do it. Early in my career, I designed integrations connecting fabrication software to CAD systems, ERP platforms, and CNC equipment — including the PowerFab–Trimble Connect 3D model viewer integration. Today, my focus is training and mentoring the next generation of developers: three engineers I've mentored have gone on to own major product areas of their own, and one now mentors others in turn.\n\nOutside of work, I co-lead a small nonprofit ministry, Projects 4 Missions, where I run donor communications, fundraising events, and teach at retreats and camps.\n\nCurrently looking for part-time (~20 hrs/week) remote or hybrid opportunities.",
